From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: Resolve Trek Tech resume page as a global

The Trek Tech shutdown score script reads gPLData through Director 4's
legacy object-call bytecode without declaring the variable global. The
original runtime resolves this reference to the movie global, but the generic
ScummVM lookup can bind it to the score-script scope and produce VOID. That
causes the preferences writer to store an empty resume page.

Limit the compatibility adjustment to Trek Tech score script 193 and its
getAt(gPLData, ...) call. Explicitly resolve that receiver as the existing
global so the current page code is written before the shutdown transition.
---
 engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp
index 857b5ad4..05d83d22 100644
--- a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp
@@ -451,7 +451,15 @@ void LC::cb_objectcall() {
 	if (nargs.u.i > 0) {
 		Datum &firstArg = g_lingo->_state->stack[g_lingo->_state->stack.size() - nargs.u.i];
 		// The first arg could be either a method name or a variable name
-		if (firstArg.type == SYMBOL) {
+		if (firstArg.type == SYMBOL &&
+				Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech") &&
+				g_lingo->_state->context && g_lingo->_state->context->_id == 193 &&
+				var.u.s->equalsIgnoreCase("getAt") &&
+				firstArg.u.s->equalsIgnoreCase("gPLData")) {
+			// Score script 193 omits its global declaration, but Director 4
+			// resolves this legacy reference to the movie's playlist global.
+			firstArg.type = GLOBALREF;
+		} else if (firstArg.type == SYMBOL) {
 			firstArg.type = VARREF;
 		}
 	}
